IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg3-public-courts`

-- bgg3-tests-public-courts: tests for bgg3-public-courts (BGG Art. 86 to 89).
-- Expected values were decided from the German text and written beside each assertion before running.

§ `Art 86 tests`

-- Art 86(1)(a) to (c): the named bodies
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(a) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the Federal Administrative Court` `Federal Administrative Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(a) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the Federal Administrative Court` `last cantonal instance` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(b) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the Federal Criminal Court` `Federal Criminal Court Complaints Chamber` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(b) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the Federal Criminal Court` `Federal Criminal Court Appeals Chamber` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(b) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the Federal Criminal Court` `another chamber of the Federal Criminal Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(b) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the Federal Criminal Court` `Federal Patent Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(c) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the independent complaints authority for radio and television` `independent complaints authority for radio and television` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(c) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the independent complaints authority for radio and television` `another body` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 86(1)(d): args (body, an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court is admissible): "sofern nicht die Beschwerde an das Bundesverwaltungsgericht zulässig ist"
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(d) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the last cantonal instance` `last cantonal instance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(d) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the last cantonal instance` `last cantonal instance` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(d) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the last cantonal instance` `another body` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1)(d) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of the last cantonal instance` `Federal Administrative Court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 86(1): args (body, an appeal to the Federal Administrative Court is admissible)
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `Federal Administrative Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `Federal Criminal Court Appeals Chamber` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `independent complaints authority for radio and television` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `last cantonal instance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `last cantonal instance` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `Federal Patent Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the appeal in public-law matters is admissible against the decision of this body` `another body` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 86(2): args (immediate lower instance is an upper court, another federal statute provides appeal from another judicial authority)
#ASSERT `Art 86(2) the immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(2) the immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(2) the immediate lower instance is an upper court, or another federal statute provides for appeal from another judicial authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 86(3): a power of the cantons
#ASSERT `Art 86(3) the canton may set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(3) the canton may set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 86(2) as a duty and Art 86(3) as a permission, run as traces (printed, not asserted: NOTES.md)
#TRACE `Art 86(2) the cantons' duty to set up an upper court as immediate lower instance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Canton DOES `set up an upper court as immediate lower instance` AT 1
#TRACE `Art 86(2) the cantons' duty to set up an upper court as immediate lower instance` AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `Art 86(3) the cantons' permission to set up an authority other than a court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Canton DOES `set up an authority other than a court as immediate lower instance` AT 1
#TRACE `Art 86(3) the cantons' permission to set up an authority other than a court` AT 0 WITH

§ `Art 87 tests`

-- Art 87(1): args (cantonal enactment, a cantonal remedy can be taken)
#ASSERT `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 87(1) the appeal lies directly against the cantonal enactment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 87(2): args (cantonal enactment, cantonal law provides a remedy against enactments)
#ASSERT `Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to the appeal against the cantonal enactment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to the appeal against the cantonal enactment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 87(2) Art 86 applies to the appeal against the cantonal enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 88 tests`

-- Art 88(1)(a): args (voting rights, election or vote; cantonal matter; act of the last cantonal instance)
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(a) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a cantonal matter against an act of the last cantonal instance` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(a) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a cantonal matter against an act of the last cantonal instance` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(a) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a cantonal matter against an act of the last cantonal instance` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(a) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a cantonal matter against an act of the last cantonal instance` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 88(1)(b): args (voting rights; federal matter; ruling of the Federal Chancellery; decision of a cantonal government)
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(b) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a federal matter against a ruling of the Federal Chancellery or a decision of a cantonal government` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(b) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a federal matter against a ruling of the Federal Chancellery or a decision of a cantonal government` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(b) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a federal matter against a ruling of the Federal Chancellery or a decision of a cantonal government` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(b) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a federal matter against a ruling of the Federal Chancellery or a decision of a cantonal government` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 88(1)(b) the appeal on voting rights is admissible in a federal matter against a ruling of the Federal Chancellery or a decision of a cantonal government` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 88(1): args (voting rights; cantonal matter; last cantonal instance; federal matter; Federal Chancellery ruling; cantonal government)
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(1) the appeal on voting rights is admissible against the act` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 88(2): args (the act can violate voters' political rights in a cantonal matter, the act is an act of the parliament or the government)
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the canton must provide a remedy against the act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the canton must provide a remedy against the act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- "Diese Pflicht erstreckt sich nicht auf Akte des Parlaments und der Regierung."
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the canton must provide a remedy against the act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 88(2) the canton must provide a remedy against the act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 88(2) as a duty of the cantons, run as a trace (printed, not asserted: NOTES.md)
#TRACE `Art 88(2) the cantons' duty to provide a remedy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Canton DOES `provide a remedy against an act that can violate voters' political rights` AT 3
#TRACE `Art 88(2) the cantons' duty to provide a remedy` AT 0 WITH

§ `Art 89 tests`

-- Art 89(1)(a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(b) the person is especially affected by the decision or enactment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(b) the person is especially affected by the decision or enactment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(c) the person has an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1)(c) the person has an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Art 89(1): args (took part, no chance, especially affected, interest worthy of protection): (a), (b) and (c) all required
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(1) the person is entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Art 89(2)(a): args (chancellery or department, subordinate service with a federal-law right, the act can violate federal legislation in its field)
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(a) the federal chancellery or department is also entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(a) the federal chancellery or department is also entitled to appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(a) the federal chancellery or department is also entitled to appeal in public-law matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(a) the federal chancellery or department is also entitled to appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 89(2)(b): args (competent body of the Federal Assembly, federal staff employment matter)
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(b) the competent body of the Federal Assembly is also entitled to appeal in a federal staff employment matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(b) the competent body of the Federal Assembly is also entitled to appeal in a federal staff employment matter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(b) the competent body of the Federal Assembly is also entitled to appeal in a federal staff employment matter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 89(2)(c): args (municipality or other public-law corporation, complains of a violation of constitutional guarantees)
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(c) the municipality or other public-law corporation is also entitled to appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(c) the municipality or other public-law corporation is also entitled to appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(c) the municipality or other public-law corporation is also entitled to appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 89(2)(d)
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(d) the person, organisation or authority is also entitled to appeal under another federal statute` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(2)(d) the person, organisation or authority is also entitled to appeal under another federal statute` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 89(3): args (voting rights matter, entitled to vote in the matter)
#ASSERT `Art 89(3) the person entitled to vote is also entitled to appeal in a voting rights matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 89(3) the person entitled to vote is also entitled to appeal in a voting rights matter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 89(3) the person entitled to vote is also entitled to appeal in a voting rights matter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
